    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0453" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/2225a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d307-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-14T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 14, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1967. You may inform the Government to which you are accredited that the
                    President has decided to send Mr. E. M.
                        House to Europe as his special representative. Mr. House will start almost immediately.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d307-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d307-f1-content">
                <p>The same to the Ambassador in Italy, No. 1764; unnumbered telegram of
                    notification on the same date to the Ambassador in France. (File No.
                    003.1140/—.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
